2026-09-27T09:58:53.8180089Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8180754Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8181175Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8182846Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8184491Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8185389Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8185605Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8185911Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8186202Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8186290Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8186499Z ================
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8186616Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8186804Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8187195Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8187422Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8187538Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8187805Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8187973Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8188110Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8188524Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8188898Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8189600Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8190139Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8190249Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8190685Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8191236Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8191528Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8192260Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8193011Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8291142Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8291897Z ========
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8292105Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8295248Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8297688Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8298100Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8298905Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8300137Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8300923Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8301545Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8302760Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8303442Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8303628Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8304030Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8304274Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8306135Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8307664Z 
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8308412Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8309402Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:58:53.8309624Z 
